Original commit body from 0d452bc4a57f183e93db14a579381833212b072e:

The per-PR gate was structurally blind to vendor hook dirs, .githooks/**,
_shared subdirs, scripts/lib/**, untracked files, and fixture-only edits,
and printed 'No Python source files changed' in every blind case. Four
closures, all over-select-never-under-select:

1. Untracked files enter change enumeration (git ls-files --others
   --exclude-standard), scoped to test/source surfaces so pending tracker
   .ops files cannot leak in and fire the fallback every run.
2. Fixture edits select their owning suite (tests/fixtures -> root suite;
   packages/X/tests/fixtures -> that package's tests). A fixture changes a
   gate's inputs without running the gate.
3. Unmapped top-level changes union the whole root suite, disclosed -
   replacing the dead CHANGED_TOP_LEVEL_SOURCES variable (defined, never
   read, documented by a comment describing a check that never existed).
4. top_level_test_map.py claims .agent/hooks/<vendor>/** via name-match
   unioned with an existence-checked parity floor (test_touch_heartbeat,
   test_session_start_respawn). .githooks/** deliberately unmapped,
   decision recorded in the docstring; the fallback covers it.

The two-sided KNOWN_UNREACHABLE ratchet now enumerates vendor dirs; three
exemptions retired. The ratchet caught its own author: the day-old
test_transcript_permissions.py was name-unreachable ('perms' is not a
prefix of 'permissions') and is renamed test_transcript_perms.py.

Route 7 (CLI-driven sole-coverer tests) stays open by design - it needs
coverage-map selection, recorded as the accepted residual on INV-kinin.

Governance: .agent/** change explicitly approved by owner (auto-pr without
--gov authorized).

